00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
NEW SONGS...NEW LAUGHS...NOW ACTION....SUSPENSE...In
The Greatest Of All Roger's Hits!

2
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
The Yellow Rose of Texas is a western, action film directed by Joseph Kane.

3
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Insurance Investigator Roy is looking for Weston and the
missing money he supposedly obtained in a robbery.

4
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
When he catches him and listens to his story, he changes his mind about him.

5
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
A freak accident locates the missing money box and they find the seal unbroken.

6
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Roy then announces the box will be opened at the showboat that evening.

7
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Roy Rogers, played by Roy Rogers.

8
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Betty Weston, played by Dale Evans.

9
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Express Agent Lucas, played by Grant Withers.

10
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Sam Weston, played by Harry Shannon.

11
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Captain 'Cap' Joe, played by George Cleveland.

12
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Charley Goss, played by Weldon Heyburn.

13
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:56,000
"The Yellow Rose of Texas" is a traditional American
song dating back to at least the 1850s.

14
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:46,000
Members of the Western Writers of America chose it as one
of the Top 100 Western songs of all time.

15
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Many versions of the song have been recorded, the most popular of
which was by Mitch Miller, whose version reached No.

16
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
1 in the United States in 1955.

17
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:16,000
Its popularity made it an unofficial state song of Texas
(the actual state song is "Texas, Our Texas").
